From 14aa7871cbef486afa525e9bdc6f0417324f8609 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dooset22 <dooset22@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:26:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] UWP: crash reports and startup diagnostics in the log

The first Xbox run exited right after creating its first graphics
pipeline without logging why. On UWP:

- Log unhandled exceptions (code, faulting module+offset, access
  violation details, call stack), std::terminate and CRT invalid
  parameter errors.
- FatalError and failed assertions write to the log before aborting;
  stderr goes nowhere on Xbox. GPU device loss ends in FatalError.
- Log the D3D12 device removed reason, the CoreWindow swap chain, the
  first presents and present failures, window open/close/resize and
  UI loop start/end.
- Flush the log after every message.
- Link the app with /MAP so crash offsets can be mapped to functions.

Also fix a race in Presenter::DXGIUITickThread, which used the shared
output pointer after unlocking the mutex instead of its local reference.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01T2Eqt3AmpbNRB9dC5uwqee
